<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 230)</h2>
<p><b>Kitsu, without the homework.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Review List from Kitsu works from an empty window</b> — it was greyed out until media was loaded, which is backwards: pulling a list is how an empty window gets its playlist. Watch Folder for Dailies is un-gated the same way.</li>
<li><b>Statuses are picks now, not vocabulary.</b> The panel asks your Kitsu instance for its task statuses and shows them by name — tick the ones that count as "awaiting review". No more typing <code>wfa,Review,pndng</code> from memory.</li>
<li>The panel remembers your project between opens, labels every field, and says when it's loading a project's playlists instead of showing a stale list.</li>
<li>Fixed: a Kitsu request arriving while another was in flight was silently dropped — a pull that did nothing, with no error. Requests queue now, and failures say so.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
